# Station hubs and arrivals StopPoints

A physical station is often several TfL StopPoints. Membership and fetch targets come from tfl-ts `STATION_HUBS`, not from matching display names.

Canonical traps: tfl-ts skill (`.claude/skills/tfl-ts/SKILL.md` in the tfl-ts package). Do not copy that essay here.

## Do

- Catalogue lines/aliases from `STATION_HUBS` + `LINE_STATION_SEQUENCES`.
- Poll with `resolveArrivalsStopId(hub, lineId)` or `resolveArrivalsStopIds(hub, tflLineIds)`.
- Restrict `tflLineIds` to keys of `LINE_STATION_SEQUENCES`. National Rail operators in a hub are topology only; polling them returns `[]`.
- Fall through blank `towards` to `destinationName` (`getNormalizedArrivals`, or the same fallback in the board).
- Explorer Tube & rail identity lists hub sibling StopPoints from static `STATION_HUBS`. Arrivals poll every sibling that carries a TfL prediction line.

## Don’t

- Merge two Naptans because they share a name (`mergeHomonyms` is for diagram label packing only).
- Poll a hub interchange id (`HUBLST`) expecting arrivals. `resolveArrivalsStopId` returns `undefined` when the line is not on that hub, not the hub id.
- Assume the Underground id at an interchange also carries Elizabeth line / Overground.

Liverpool Street: `940GZZLULVT` (tube) and `910GLIVST` (Elizabeth + Weaver). Waterloo: do not poll `910GWATRLMN` for Bakerloo.